0..77 Comment "// The lists of pairwise distinct naturals are an inductive-recursive family."
78..107 Comment "// The family is no universe."
108..110 Comment "//"
111..184 Comment "// A cons holds evidence of its head\'s freshness for its tail. A function"
185..257 Comment "// computes the type of that evidence from the tail. The lists and their"
258..291 Comment "// freshness thus form one block."
292..294 Comment "//"
295..372 Comment "// Freshness recurses on the list. Each arm binds its two types by a run. The"
373..446 Comment "// arm then returns their pair. The pair is data. The arm returns it as a"
447..455 Comment "// term."
456..458 Comment "//"
459..538 Comment "// - see: #3572 — not implemented: the pair\'s types written as calls in place"
539..619 Comment "// - see: `pathological/universe/fresh-lists.gandr` — the pair\'s types written"
620..642 Comment "//   in place, refused"
643..697 Comment "// - see: the Agda standard library, `Data.List.Fresh`"
699..715 Comment "// The naturals."
